QuestGuidance.Register("en",231,{
[7361]="70057545\n1\tTalk to Léothred\tTalk to Léothred.\n2\tListen to Léothred's tale\tListen to Léothred's tale.\n3\tTalk to Léothred\tTalk to Léothred.\n4\tListen to Léothred's tale\tListen to Léothred's tale.\n",
[7362]="7000E908\n1\tTalk to Kaj\tTalk to Kaj.\n2\tPrevent Pinja's brothers from interrupting Kaj\tPinja has three brothers. Make sure they do not interrupt Kaj's ritual.\n3\tTalk to Manu\tCalm the mammoth and prevent it from rampaging\n4\tTame the mammoth\tManu has returned with a wild mammoth in tow. You should help calm the wild beast.\n5\tTalk to Manu\tManu demands your attention.\n6\tTalk to Pinja\tPinja seems to have been impressed by Kaj's bravery\n",
[7363]="7005B24F\n1\tTalk to Klúso\tKlúso is ready to describe what he saw earlier. You should talk to Klúso.\n2\tFollow Klúso\tKlúso is describing what he saw transpire between the hobgoblins and ice-giants. You should follow Klúso.\n3\tFollow the hobgoblins to listen to the conversation\tKlúso is describing what he saw transpire between the hobgoblins and ice-giants. You should follow the hobgoblins to listen to the conversation.\n4\tListen to the conversation\tKlúso is describing what he saw transpire between the hobgoblins and ice-giants. You should listen to the conversation.\n5\tReturn to Klúso\tKlúso is concluding his story. You should return to him.\n",
[7364]="700097E6\n1\tDefeat Idella Crypt-breaker\tIdella Crypt-breaker is somewhere within the depths of the tomb of Elendil. Calenglad was right -- Idella Crypt-breaker's gang of tomb-robbers has taken advantage of the newly-lowered waters to plumb the depths of the tomb for treasure. She must be stopped.\n2\tTalk to Gwindeth\tGwindeth has come to the Tomb of Elendil, and is waiting to speak with you in its deepest chamber. You have dispatched Idella Crypt-breaker, but there is no sign of the Silithar.\n3\tFind the Silithar\tThe Silithar is somewhere in the caverns beneath the tomb of Elendil. You did not find the Silithar in the final chamber of the tomb of Elendil -- it must have been carried somewhere by the retreating waters.\n4\tTalk to Gwindeth\tGwindeth is now in the cave beneath the tomb of Elendil. You have recovered the Silithar, and Gwindeth waits to speak with you.\n",
[7365]="70021A49\n1\tRecover a crude key from the guards\tSeek out guards within the cavern and recover a crude key from them.\n2\tUnlock the cell door for a prisoner\tDiscover and open a locked cell with the crude key that you recovered.\n3\tRelease the first captive.\t\n4\tRecover a crude key from the guards\tSeek out guards within the cavern and recover a crude key from them.\n5\tUnlock the cell door for a prisoner\tDiscover and open a locked cell with the crude key that you recovered.\n6\tRelease the second captive.\t\n7\tRecover a crude key from the guards\tSeek out guards within the cavern and recover a crude key from them.\n8\tUnlock the cell door for the last prisoner\tDiscover and open a locked cell with the crude key that you recovered.\n9\tRelease the last captive.\t\n10\tDefeat Laodegan near the entrance\tThe Houndmaster Laodegan has heard that an outsider has attacked the dungeon and is guarding the entrance.\n",
[7366]="700156C4\n1\tDefeat Orkish recruits (total: 12)\030Defeat the Uruk Battle-master\tYou must defeat the Orkish recruits before they are prepared to launch their offensive against the dwarves and defeat the Uruk who is overseeing their training.\n2\tUse the ancient anvil\030Collect Infused Garnet\tUse the ancient forge to empower your infused garnet.\n",
[7367]="7002EF80\n1\tDefend the herd from attacking Orcs\tDefend the herd from attacking Orcs.\n2\tConfront Shadowfax\tShadowfax is at the centre of the wild herd. You should confront Shadowfax.\n",
[7368]="70054D0F\n1\tFind the artifact\tFind the artifact.\n2\tDestroy the Orb of Madness\tDestroy the Orb of Madness.\n3\tOvercome the Trial of Madness\tOvercome the Trial of Madness.\n",
[7369]="70054D10\n1\tDefeat the Ghâsh-hai\tDefeat the Ghâsh-hai.\n2\tDestroy of the Orb of Wrath\tDestroy the Orb of Wrath.\n3\tOvercome the Trial of Wrath\tOvercome the Trial of Wrath.\n",
[7370]="7005B50B\n1\tTalk to Féli\tFéli is waiting for you before he starts the interrogation.\n2\tListen to the interrogation\tYou should follow Féli to the interrogation and see what happens.\n3\tTalk to Shúkurz\tYou should continue interrogating Shúkurz.\n4\tTalk to Shúkurz\tYou should continue interrogating Shúkurz.\n5\tTalk to the Orc captain\tYou should talk to the Orc captain.\n6\tFill weapon barrels (total: 3)\030Deliver orders to Orc soldiers (total: 3)\tThere are empty weapon barrels and Orc soldiers waiting on orders throughout the camp. You should fill the barrels and deliver orders.\n7\tReturn to Shúkurz and listen to his story\tYou should return to Shúkurz and continue listening to his story.\n8\tTalk to Shúkurz\tYou should continue interrogating Shúkurz.\n9\tWatch events unfold\tYou should watch the events before you unfold.\n10\tDefeat the hobgoblin raiders\tYou should defeat the hobgoblin raiders.\n11\tTalk to Shúkurz\tYou should continue interrogating Shúkurz.\n12\tTalk to Shúkurz\tYou should continue interrogating Shúkurz.\n13\tListen to the interrogation\tYou should continue observing the interrogation.\n14\tTalk to Náin\tNáin wishes to speak with you.\n",
[7371]="70009DD9\n1\tSpeak with Longbough\tYou should speak with Longbough and aid him against the Twisted Heart.\n2\tTalk to Longbough\tYou should speak with Longbough.\n",
[7372]="700010FA\n1\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas is following a mysterious trail into the Gladdalf. You and Legolas of Mirkwood have followed the signs of the Wood-trolls through the wilderness of the Trollshaws.\n2\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas is threatened by attacking wood-trolls in the Gladdalf. You and Legolas of Mirkwood have followed the signs of the wood-trolls through the wilderness of the Trollshaws.\n3\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas is following a mysterious trail into the Gladdalf. You and Legolas of Mirkwood have followed the signs of the wood-trolls through the wilderness of the Trollshaws.\n4\tAid Legolas\tLegolas is threatened by droves of corrupted fen-crawlers in the Gladdalf. You and Legolas of Mirkwood have followed the signs of the Wood-trolls through the wilderness of the Trollshaws.\n5\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas has followed a mysterious trail onto an earthen rise surrounded by water in the centre of the Gladdalf. You and Legolas the Elf have followed the signs of the Wood-trolls through the wilderness of the Trollshaws.\n6\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas is waiting to speak with you. You and Legolas of Mirkwood have followed the signs of the wood-trolls through the wilderness of the Trollshaws.\n",
[7373]="700571AE\n1\tTalk to Vaskorn\tTalk to Vaskorn.\n2\tFind and defeat Khilbakh\030Defeat the raiding party\tFind and defeat Khilbakh and the Warg raiding party. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[7374]="7006EF57\n1\tTalk to Jajax\tJajax is in one of the cages of the Fleetfast gaol.\n2\tRemain alert\tThere is a commotion outside the cage in the Fleetfast gaol.\n3\tTalk to Belondor in the Fleetfast gaol\tBelondor and Rothog have come to free you from the Fleetfast gaol.\n4\tTalk to Jajax\tJajax is in the Fleetfast gaol.\n5\tSearch the bodies of the slain guards for the keys to the gaol\tJajax has suggested that you search the bodies of the slain guards to see if either of them have the keys to the gaol.\n6\tSearch the bodies of the slain guards for the keys to the gaol\tJajax has suggested that you search the bodies of the slain guards to see if either of them have the keys to the gaol.\n7\tMake your way downstairs to the hatch leading to Umbar-môkh\tBelondor and Rothog entered the gaol from a hatch downstairs that leads to Umbar-môkh. Now you should find your way downstairs to escape!\n8\tTalk to Tatháta in the Fleetfast gaol\tTatháta stands by the hatch leading to Umbar-môkh.\n9\tTalk to Belondor in the Fleetfast gaol\tBelondor stands by the hatch leading to Umbar-môkh.\n10\tTalk to Tatháta in the Fleetfast gaol\tTatháta stands by the hatch leading to Umbar-môkh.\n11\tDescend into Umbar-môkh\tThe path of your escape leads into Umbar-môkh.\n12\tTalk to Jajax in Umbar-môkh\tYou and Jajax have escaped from the gaol, but there are foes between you and the hidden harbour.\n13\tMake your way to the hidden harbour\tYour foes now defeated, the way to the hidden harbour is open to you.\n14\tBoard Tatháta's ship and go belowdecks\tYou should board Tatháta's ship so you may pursue the Song.\n15\tTalk to Jajax in the ship Sotóka\030Talk to Belondor in the ship Sotóka\030Talk to Rothog in the ship Sotóka\tYour allies stand ready to pursue the Song.\n16\tTalk to Tatháta in her ship Sotóka\tYour allies stand ready to pursue the Song.\n17\tPursue the Song to Gondor\tYour pursuit of the Song begins.\n",
[7375]="70059B15\n1\tTalk to Durin\tPrince Durin stands at the Thing-fold to begin the Dwarrowmoot for which he has called.\n2\tObserve the Dwarrowmoot\tThe Dwarrowmoot has begun.\n3\tRemain on your guard!\tThe Dwarrowmoot has been interrupted by the dragon!\n4\tRemain on your guard!\tThe Dwarrowmoot has been interrupted by the dragon!\n5\tStand with the dwarves\tHrímil has escaped on powerful wings, making for the high peak, but her terror is plain to see.\n6\tTalk to Durin\tThe Dwarrowmoot came to a sudden end, but Durin has made a decision: it is time to face the dragon and reclaim the Mountain-home!\n",
[7376]="70061C17\n1\tTalk to Meneldir in Crossway House\tMeneldir wants to speak with you in Crossway House while you wait for the hours to pass.\n2\tTalk to Maddoc at the counter\030Talk to Bledri upstairs\030Talk to Aldyth upstairs\030Talk to Aberthol in the main room\tMeneldir has asked you to speak with some of the townsfolk who gather within Crossway House, and to assure them that they will be safe.\n3\tReturn to your table\tThe residents of Herne are in fairly high spirits considering the dangers that may threaten their town.\n4\tSit at Meneldir's table\tMeneldir has invited you to sit at his table.\n5\tListen to the conversation of your companions\tListen to the conversation of your companions and remain on guard.\n6\tTalk to Boromir at the windows\tBoromir stands at one of the windows. Has he seen anything outside?\n7\tListen to the conversation of your companions\tListen to the conversation of your companions and remain on guard.\n8\tTalk to Boromir\tBoromir wears a concerned expression.\n9\tListen to the conversation of your companions\tListen to the conversation of your companions and remain on guard.\n10\tGo outside Crossway House and investigate\tA feeling of dread has settled upon Crossway House. What has happened outside?\n11\tTalk to Meneldir outside Crossway House\tYour companions stand ready to defend the folk of Herne. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[7377]="70053B2E\n1\tTalk to Vágari the Wanderer\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n2\tListen to the shade's account\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n3\tTalk to Vágari the Wanderer\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n4\tListen to Vágari's account\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n5\tTalk to Vágari the Wanderer\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n6\tListen to Vágari's account\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n7\tTalk to Rioc\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n",
[7378]="70058C80\n1\tTalk to Nagli\tNagli can be found at Khadâsh-gâra. You should talk to Nagli.\n2\tFollow Nagli\tNagli can be found at Khadâsh-gâra. You should follow Nagli.\n3\tSit on the log beside Nagli at the camp-fire at Khadâsh-gâra\tA suitable log for sitting can be found beside Nagli at Khadâsh-gâra. Nagli has asked you to join him and the other Want-kin at the camp-fire at Khadâsh-gâra.\n4\tListen to Nagli and the Want-kin\tThe Want-kin are preparing to have supper.\n5\tShare a hearty supper with the Want-kin at Khadâsh-gâra\tNagli set your supper beside you at Khadâsh-gâra. The Want-kin have begun their meal. You should share a supper with them.\n6\tTalk to Nagli\tNagli can be found at Khadâsh-gâra. Nagli has asked to speak with you. You should talk to Nagli.\n7\tCollect firewood to stoke the fire at Khadâsh-gâra\tFirewood can be found at Khadâsh-gâra. Nagli has asked you to fetch some firewood to stoke the fire at Khadâsh-gâra. You should collect the firewood.\n8\tTalk to Nagli\tNagli can be found at Khadâsh-gâra. You have brought more firewood to the fire at Khadâsh-gâra as Nagli asked. You should talk to Nagli.\n9\tTell Nagli and the Want-kin the story of your adventures before coming to Elderslade\tNagli can be found at Khadâsh-gâra. Nagli has asked to hear more tales of your adventures before coming to Elderslade. You should tell Nagli and the Want-kin of your adventures in Middle-earth. NOTE: You will need to select Nagli before emoting to advance this quest.\n10\tListen to Nagli and Stórath\tNagli and Stórath are talking about the tales you told.\n11\tTalk to Nagli\tNagli can be found at Khadâsh-gâra. After Stórath expressed his displeasure in hosting you, Nagli and the other Want-kin defended your presence at Khadâsh-gâra. You should talk to Nagli.\n",
[7379]="70058427\n1\tTalk to Durin during the assault on Zarkul-sulûn\tPrince Durin has commanded that the Gabil'akkâ seize the ruin of Zarkul-sulûn from the Orcs.\n",
[7380]="7005BEA2\n1\tTalk to Hórin\tHórin is standing by with the dwarf forces. You should talk to Hórin.\n2\tFind the hobgoblins\tYou have tracked the hobgoblins to the end of the road. You should follow Hórin and find the hobgoblins.\n3\tFollow Hórin to the hiding spot\tYou have tracked the hobgoblins to the end of the road. You should follow Hórin and find the hobgoblins.\n4\tListen to the conversation\tYou have found Gorgar at the end of the road. He must be the hobgoblins' reason for coming here! You should watch and listen as events unfold!\n5\tReturn to the Gate of Uzdarulzahar\tThe hobgoblins will soon be upon you! You should return to the Gate of Uzdarulzahar and summon your forces!\n6\tBlow the horn to summon your forces!\tThe hobgoblins will soon be upon you! You should blow the horn to summon your forces!\n7\tWait for your forces to arrive\tThe hobgoblins will soon be upon you! You should wait for your forces to arrive!\n",
[7381]="7004E640\n1\tTalk to Bótuz Frostblood\tBótuz Frostblood and his Zhélruka have crossed Óinsbridge in search of Karazgar.\n2\tSearch for Karazgar with Bótuz and his warriors\tBótuz Frostblood and his Zhélruka have crossed Óinsbridge in search of Karazgar.\n3\tRemain alert for any treachery by Karazgar\tBótuz Frostblood and his Zhélruka have crossed Óinsbridge in search of Karazgar.\n4\tTalk to Karazgar, but remain alert for treachery\tKarazgar has asked to speak with you.\n5\tRemain alert for any treachery by Karazgar\tBótuz Frostblood and his Zhélruka have crossed Óinsbridge in search of Karazgar.\n6\tTalk to Bótuz Frostblood\tBótuz Frostblood has some words for you now that Karazgar has departed.\n",
[7382]="70053A11\n1\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn has agreed to tell you what he knows of Eärnur's last days.\n2\tListen to the words of Aragorn concerning Eärnur\tAragorn has agreed to tell you what he knows of Eärnur's last days.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn has agreed to tell you what he knows of Eärnur's last days.\n4\tListen to the words of Aragorn\tAragorn has agreed to tell you what he knows of King Eärnur's last days.\n5\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn has agreed to tell you what he knows of King Eärnur's last days.\n",
[7383]="700115FE\n1\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is on the slope that leads up to the pool before the Doors of Durin. Bósi is waiting to wish you well against the Watcher in the Water. He is confident that the sharp bite of your weapon will prevail.\n2\tTalk to Bósi's scout\tBósi sent some dwarves up to the pool to scout ahead for the beast. Armed with your new weapon, you are ready to face the Watcher in the Water.\n3\tDrive off the Watcher in the Water\tThe Watcher in the Water lurks within the pool, casting its arms forth to attack you! You must defeat the arms of the Watcher and drive it from the entrance to Moria.\n4\tTalk to Brogur\tBrogur has come to the shore of the Black Pool, against his cousin's wishes.\n5\tProtect Brogur from the Watcher in the Water\tBrogur has challenged the Watcher in the Water, determined to avenge the death of his son. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tTalk to Bósi\030Talk to Brogur\tBósi and Brogur are on the edge of the pool. The Watcher in the Water has been driven off, and you should now speak with Bósi and Brogur.\n",
[7384]="700579FB\n1\tTalk to Merethien\tMerethien, the Master Foodmonger of Minas Tirith, has some questions for Merry and Pippin concerning what qualifies as a 'banquet' at their home, the distant Shire. Furthermore, she is pleased to have an excuse to leave Ioreth's chatter and Galathir's lecture behind her.\n2\tTalk to Merry\tMerethien wants to know if Merry and Pippin are satisfied that the wedding-feast she has helped to prepare can compare with the banquets they described in the Shire.\n3\tFollow Pippin back to his table\tPippin wants to return to his own table for a bit, and wishes for you and Merry to follow him.\n4\tTalk to Beregond\tBeregond and his family sit at Pippin's table with a number of Gondorian nobles.\n5\tTalk to Thrymm Red-beard\tThrymm Red-beard has obtained a captive audience, and is regaling them with tales of his adventures.\n6\tListen (again) to Thrymm's tale of his exploits\tThrymm Red-beard has obtained a captive audience, and is regaling them with tales of his adventures.\n7\tTalk to Prince Imrahil\tPrince Imrahil was given a message for you.\n8\tTalk to the wine steward downstairs\tPrince Imrahil told you a wine steward working at the wedding-feast wanted you to meet with him downstairs.\n9\tGo outside and confront the 'rough sorts' described by the wine steward\tThe wine steward gave you some fine bottles of Gondor's finest to use as a peace offering with the 'rough sorts' gathering outside. You have been tasked with leaving Merethrond by the front doors and confronting the group of rough sorts the wine steward described.\n10\tListen to the words of the Grey Company\tThe Grey Company has gathered to celebrate the wedding of their chieftain, and to honour the great deeds done on his behalf.\n11\tTalk to Radanir\030Talk to Culang\tThe Grey Company has gathered to celebrate the wedding of their chieftain, and to honour the great deeds done on his behalf.\n12\tGo back inside Merethrond and rejoin the wedding-feast\tYou should return to the wedding-feast, which will likely soon be winding down.\n13\tTalk to the wine steward\tThe wine steward is being regaled with tales of Thrymm's heroics, and he wishes to speak with you.\n14\tTalk to King Elessar upstairs, on the western side of the feast-hall\tThe wedding-feast continues into the night and you should speak with King Elessar before the festivities conclude.\n15\tTalk to Prince Faramir of Ithilien\tPrince Faramir of Ithilien is at the head table in Merethrond.\n16\tTalk to Samwise Gamgee\tSamwise Gamgee is at the head table in Merethrond.\n17\tInvestigate the disturbance on the western side of the feast-hall\tA loud disturbance has caused a commotion on the western side of the feast-hall.\n18\tTalk to King Elessar\tKing Elessar wishes to speak with you.\n",
[7385]="7004D3D9\n1\tTalk to Bryn\tTry to speak with Bryn.\n2\tFollow Bryn to meet his friend\tFollow Bryn and meet his friend.\n3\tListen to Bryn's exchange with Akshir\tListen to Bryn's exchange with Akshir.\n4\tBeckon Bryn to you\tBeckon Bryn to you.\n5\tListen to the Weeping Warrior\tListen to the Weeping Warrior.\n6\tTalk to Bryn\tTalk to Bryn.\n",
[7386]="700143E0\n1\tTalk to Bori\tBori is waiting to speak with you concerning his plan.\n2\tWave at Bori to demonstrate the signal\030Stand near Bori\tBori is waiting for you to wave so he will know that you understand the signal.\n3\tFollow Bori\tBori has asked you to follow him into Stazgnâkh.\n4\tTalk to Bori\tBori is looking out into the darkness that surrounds Stazgnâkh and is waiting to speak with you.\n5\tWave for Bori to follow when the coast is clear\030Get to the side of the building without being seen\tThe building for which you should run is straight ahead of Bori's position, built into the side of the rock wall. Be sure to stay away from the patrolling Orcs, or your mission will end in failure.\n6\tWait for Bori to arrive\tBori is making his way deeper into Stazgnâkh.\n7\tWave for Bori to follow when the coast is clear\030Get to beneath the tracks without being seen\tThe mine cart tracks for which you should run are straight ahead of Bori's position, built above a gap in the rock wall. Be sure to stay away from the patrolling Orcs, or your mission will end in failure.\n8\tWait for Bori to arrive\tBori is making his way deeper into Stazgnâkh.\n9\tWait for the Orcs to leave Stazgnâkh\tBori's plan is in full effect; it is now up to the valiant efforts of Wíli and Stilling to draw the main force of the Orcs out of the encampment.\n10\tTalk to Bori\tBori is waiting beneath the mine cart tracks to speak with you about the main force of the Orcs.\n11\tWave for Bori to follow when the coast is clear\030Get to beneath the platform without being seen\tThe platform for which you should run is straight ahead of Bori's position, built above a gap in the rock wall. Be sure to stay away from the patrolling Orcs, or your mission will end in failure.\n12\tWait for Bori to arrive\tBori is making his way deeper into Stazgnâkh.\n13\tWave for Bori to follow when the coast is clear\030Get to the scaffolding without being seen\tThe scaffolding for which you should run is straight ahead of Bori's position; he wants you to wait for him in its shadow. Be sure to stay away from the patrolling Orcs, or your mission will end in failure.\n14\tWait for Bori to arrive\tBori is making his way deeper into Stazgnâkh.\n15\tTalk to Bori\tThe time has come to shed all stealth; you and Bori are now deep enough into the camp that the leader of the White Hand Orcs is without the safety of his protectors!\n",
[7387]="70022474\n1\tTalk to the stag-spirit\tSpeak with the stag-spirit and confront its challenge.\n2\tAccept the stag-spirit's challenge\tAccept the stag-spirit's challenge of wisdom.\n3\tIdentify the spirit of Wisdom\tFive spirits stand before you. One is the spirit of Wisdom, the other four are spirits of Anger, Greed, Vengeance, and Fear. You must find the spirit of Wisdom among them -- but decide carefully for your choice is perilous. The stag-spirit told you this: Firstly, you must know that Fear can be found directly to the right of Vengeance. Secondly, you must know that Anger is directly left of Greed. Lastly, the spirit of Wisdom cannot be found next to Greed, Anger, or Vengeance. Choose wisely. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tAfter speaking with the Stag-spirit, you must drink from the strange pool to escape from this eerie realm of spirits.\t\n",
[7388]="70022477\n1\tChallenge Gwenaewen's spirit\tApproach the falcon-spirit and prove your quickness in following it.\n2\tFollow the spirit to the first lith\tYou must follow Gwenaewen's spirit!\n3\tFollow the spirit to the second lith\tYou must follow Gwenaewen's spirit!\n4\tFollow the spirit to the third lith\tYou must follow Gwenaewen's spirit!\n5\tFollow the spirit to the fourth lith\tYou must follow Gwenaewen's spirit!\n6\tFollow the spirit to the mystic pool\tYou must follow Gwenaewen's spirit!\n7\tAfter speaking with the Falcon-spirit, you must drink from the strange pool to escape from this eerie realm of spirits.\t\n",
[7389]="70022473\n1\tChallenge the boar-spirit\tApproach the ancient spirit and prove your strength in challenge against it.\n2\tAfter speaking with the Boar-spirit, you must drink from the strange pool to escape from this eerie realm of spirits.\t\n",
[7390]="70022472\n1\tChallenge the ox-spirit\tThe ox-spirit has set before you a challenge of endurance. You must both survive against the waves of crushing despair before you.\n2\tHaving faced your challenge and emerged unbowed, you may now return to the waking world through the waters of the pool.\t\n",
[7391]="700272DB\n1\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad is on the path leading up to Tûr Morva.\n2\tTalk to Léolin\tLéolin is on the path leading up to Tûr Morva.\n3\tFollow Léolin into Tûr Morva\tLéolin is leading you up the hill to meet with Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva.\n4\tTalk to Saeradan\tSaeradan has been hit by a stone thrown by a Dunlending. You should check to make sure that he is all right.\n5\tTalk to Mair\tMair is not pleased at whoever threw the rock at Saeradan.\n6\tFollow Léolin through Tûr Morva\tLéolin is leading you through Tûr Morva to meet with Lheu Brenin, the leader of the Falcon-clan.\n7\tTalk to Penrod\tLheu Brenin's first Brehur, Penrod, is ready to speak with you.\n8\tMeet with Lheu Brenin, leader of the Falcon-clan\tYou have come into Tûr Morva to meet with Lheu Brenin, leader of the Falcon-clan.\n9\tTalk to Lheu Brenin\tLheu Brenin is waiting to speak with you.\n10\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[7392]="7004729B\n1\tTalk to King Elessar on the slope of Mindolluin\tYou have come with King Elessar and Mithrandir to a secret path high above Minas Tirith.\n2\tRemain alert for any sign of danger\tYou have come with King Elessar and Mithrandir to a secret path high above Minas Tirith, on the slopes of Mount Mindolluin.\n3\tFind the sapling amid the snows atop Mindolluin\tA sapling grows by the snow line high atop Mount Mindolluin.\n4\tTalk to King Elessar on Mindolluin\tKing Elessar is by the young sapling atop Mindolluin.\n5\tTalk to Mithrandir on Mindolluin\tMithrandir is by the young sapling atop Mindolluin.\n",
})
